hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15830","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar informed us, from Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Said ibn al-Salt, from Suhayl Ibn al-Bayda, he said: While we were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I was riding behind him, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Suhayl Ibn al-Bayda, and he raised his voice two or three times, each time Suhayl answered him. The people heard the voice of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and thought he meant them, so those ahead were held back and those behind caught up, until when they gathered the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah, Allah forbids him to the Fire and makes Paradise obligatory for him."
"15831","Harun narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Haywah narrated to me: Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, from Said ibn al-Salt, from Suhayl Ibn al-Bayda of Banu Abd al-Dar, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and he mentioned its meaning."
"15933","My father narrated to me, from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Zuhri, he said: I heard my father narrating from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Suhayl Ibn Bayda, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called one night while I was riding behind him: O Suhayl Ibn Bayda, raising his voice with it repeatedly until those behind us and before us heard. So they gathered and knew he wanted to speak something: That whoever says there is no god but Allah, Allah the Mighty and Majestic makes Paradise obligatory for him by it and frees him by it from the Fire."
"15934","Harun narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said, Haywa narrated to me, Yazid ibn al-Had narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Sa'id ibn al-Salt, from Suhayl Ibn al-Bayda of Banu Abd al-Dar, he said: While we were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned its meaning."
